    "availability": {
      "en": "Ninety megohms in the probe body, dividing against the meter's own ten. The meter honestly reads a tenth and the panel puts the ten back, so the number on the wall is the node's — and the divider underneath it is being loaded ten times more lightly than the bare meter loads it."
    }
  }
